1
00:00:00,000 --> 00:00:10,960
If cold air, dry air, or a sudden weather change makes your nose run or clog up — even though your allergy tests come back negative — you might be dealing with vasomotor rhinitis, not a typical allergy.

2
00:00:11,280 --> 00:00:14,720
Vasomotor rhinitis isn't triggered by a specific allergen at all.

3
00:00:15,040 --> 00:00:20,000
The blood vessels inside your nasal lining just overreact to nonspecific triggers instead.

4
00:00:20,320 --> 00:00:25,440
Temperature swings, dry indoor air, and strong smells are three of the most common ones.

5
00:00:25,760 --> 00:00:27,360
First, temperature swings.

6
00:00:27,680 --> 00:00:38,320
Stepping from a heated or air-conditioned room into the opposite temperature outside makes the vessels in your nasal lining suddenly dilate, and congestion or a runny nose can hit within minutes.

7
00:00:38,640 --> 00:00:47,760
Layering up before you go outside, and covering your nose and mouth with a scarf in cold weather, gives your nasal lining time to adjust instead of reacting all at once.

8
00:00:48,080 --> 00:00:56,800
Second, dry indoor air from heating or air conditioning dries out the nasal lining, which makes it even more reactive to every other trigger on this list.

9
00:00:57,120 --> 00:01:05,680
Running a humidifier to keep indoor humidity between 40 and 60 percent, and using a saline nasal spray, keeps the lining from drying out in the first place.

10
00:01:06,000 --> 00:01:17,760
Third, strong smells like perfume, cleaning products, or cigarette smoke, along with stress and sudden emotional shifts, can set off the exact same nerve response — with no allergen involved at all.

11
00:01:18,080 --> 00:01:24,560
Regular allergy medication often doesn't touch this kind of rhinitis, which is exactly why it gets missed for so long.

12
00:01:24,880 --> 00:01:39,440
Doctors more often reach for azelastine, an intranasal antihistamine, or budesonide, a nasal steroid spray, both of which are approved specifically for nonallergic rhinitis, along with an ipratropium bromide spray for a persistently runny nose.

13
00:01:39,760 --> 00:01:47,360
Buffering temperature swings, keeping indoor air humid, and steering clear of your specific triggers cut down flare-ups noticeably.

14
00:01:47,680 --> 00:01:58,800
If congestion or a runny nose sticks around for more than a few weeks despite that, talk to an ENT about a targeted nasal spray instead of reaching for another allergy pill that was never going to work in the first place.
